  "documents": [
    {
      "id": "northwind-fairness-policy-cbe85d6003",
      "path": "docs/policy/northwind-fairness-policy.md",
      "sha256": "d95f246d5fa15b6c13d7ae927efb03130c6a59be8b1befd6e6b53e856fcf0470",
      "bytes": 931,
      "lines": 35,
      "body": "# Northwind Support — Fairness and Access Policy\n\nNorthwind classifies inbound support tickets. This policy covers the model that does it.\n\n## Data provenance\n\nData sources are listed in /policies/support-intake. We do not train on ticket bodies\nwritten by customers.\n\n## Retention\n\nWe retain ticket transcripts for 400 days. Retention period for audit logs is 400 days.\n\n## Human oversight\n\nHuman review is available on request for any classification a customer disputes.\nWe review monthly samples for consistency.\n\n## Consent and redress\n\nAn appeal is available for 60 days. Consent is required before a transcript is used for\ntraining.\n\n## Accountability\n\nAn audit trail of every classification is available to the internal audit team.\n\n## Fairness\n\nWe monitor subgroup disparity across language, region and account age.\n\n## Transparency\n\nInterpretability is not currently available to customers; we document this limitation.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "meridian-system-card-7eddbf4fcb",
      "path": "docs/policy/meridian-system-card.md",
      "sha256": "84886b856ea1ac51cbf444732297a606f41f75896dcbd23170c58a0d1db7db0b",
      "bytes": 766,
      "lines": 28,
      "body": "# Meridian Lending — System Card\n\nMeridian decides credit-limit changes for existing customers. We publish the decision\npolicy at /policies/credit-limit-v4.\n\n## Data and training\n\n- Data sources are listed in appendix A. We never train on applicant-uploaded documents.\n- We retain application events for 2555 days.\n\n## Human oversight\n\nHuman review is available for every adverse decision within two business days.\nWe monitor override rates monthly.\n\n## Redress\n\nAn appeal is available for 30 days after a decision. Opt out is available in settings.\n\n## Transparency\n\nExplainability is available as a per-decision reason code. We measure subgroup disparity\nacross four cohorts.\n\n## Known limitations\n\nWe do not offer an appeal route for automated identity checks.\n"
    }
  ],
